# OpenSpec (Synapse-native)

Do **not** use the npm `@fission-ai/openspec` CLI. Use MCP tools + `syn openspec`.

## Slash commands (on-demand only)

Install with `syn openspec init` or say yes during `syn init`. Invoke only when the user types `/`:

| Slash (Cursor) | Purpose |
|----------------|---------|
| `/opsx-explore` | Investigate codebase — read-only |
| `/opsx-new` | Scaffold change folder only (step-by-step planning) |
| `/opsx-continue` | Next planning artifact (expanded flow) |
| `/opsx-ff` | Fast-forward all planning artifacts |
| `/opsx-propose` | Create `openspec/changes/<id>/` + artifacts |
| `/opsx-apply` | Implement tasks (TDD) + workflow |
| `/opsx-sync` | Merge delta specs → `openspec/specs/` |
| `/opsx-verify` | Quality gate before archive |
| `/opsx-archive` | Archive change + sync specs |

Definitions: `.cursor/commands/opsx-*.md`

## When to suggest OpenSpec (no slash)

- New features, large refactors, architecture changes, release gates
- **Not** required for typos or 1–2 file fixes

## MCP reference flow

1. `openspec_router` → flow (`sdd`, `bugfix`, …)
2. `openspec_propose`
3. `openspec_apply` + `start_workflow: true`
4. Implement + `workflow_next`
5. `openspec_verify`
6. `openspec_sync` / `openspec_archive`
7. `syn migrate` — re-index brain

CLI: `syn openspec init | verify | sync`

Checklist: [docs/CHECKLIST-OPENSPEC-CODEGRAPH.md](docs/CHECKLIST-OPENSPEC-CODEGRAPH.md)
